  <link:footnoteLink xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/link" xlink:type="extended">
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-1" id="fn-1" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">A cash distribution of available earnings and return of capital to the sole member totaling $45 million was approved by the Board of Managers on March 30, 2026. With this distribution, the total distributions for 2026 are $45 million.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-2" id="fn-2" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ASC 740 considers the equity component of AFUDC a temporary difference for which deferred income taxes must be provided. The Company is required to record the deferred tax liability for AFUDC equity in Account 282 with a corresponding regulatory asset. The regulatory asset is itself a temporary difference for which deferred income taxes are recognized and recorded in Account 283.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-3" id="fn-3" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1986, by its Section 3401(a)(1), requires the Commission to assess and collect fees and annual charges in any fiscal year in amounts equal to all of the costs incurred by the Commission in a fiscal year. For the purposes of recovering this payment, this Section establishes a FERC ACA Unit Charge to be applicable to all jurisdictional transportation quantities transported. These costs will continue to be recovered under its current rates with customers.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-4" id="fn-4" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This balance represents the impact of U.S. Tax Reform as applied to businesses subject to rate-regulated accounting. The regulatory liability will be amortized over varying terms that approximate the expected reversal of the underlying deferred tax assets and liabilities that gave rise to the regulatory liability.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate schedule PAL is a balancing service; therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing do not represent gas delivered.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other Gas Uses include, but are not limited to, Flow Tests, Blowing Drips, Running Pigs/Spheres, Blowing Down Lines, Compressor Station Blowdowns and Heaters.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Retainage volumes reported by Respondent are actual volumes retained by contract type (Discounted, Negotiated, or Recourse.)</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Respondent uses a monthly average spot rate as the basis for valuing gas.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Respondent cannot track Gas Used or Lost and Unaccounted For by contract type. Both Gas Used and Lost and Unaccounted for are allocated between contract type on the basis of actual retainage volumes recorded on RAM rate schedules.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Respondent has a Commission-approved Retainage Adjustment Mechanism (RAM) that tracks shipper supplied gas. Any excess or deficient balance is included in the next annual filing and collected or passed back, as appropriate, through a change in the surcharge.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate schedule PAL is a balancing service; therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing do not represent gas delivered.</link:footnote>
